    <selectionEntryGroup name="Army Specializations" id="63e4-c84a-dbda-2337" hidden="false">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="13th KuK Landwehr Infantry Division (Wien)	" id="f340-7eb5-dc73-7f37" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="1" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Noble Authority" id="cf27-8419-6fdb-908e" hidden="false">
              <description>Command Units in your army are always considered Ordered.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Reichsstandschaft" id="c9f4-9011-5e24-6326" hidden="false">
              <description>When a Grand Ordeal is completed by a Command Unit, gain 1 VP


Each Ordeal can only be accomplished once per game.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Grand Ordeals" id="cec1-6f9c-26c3-8be5" hidden="false">
              <description>* Kill an enemy command unit or an enemy Model with 10 or more health.
+1 VP if that Unit was the Field Commander


* Capture an objective outside of your Deployment Zone.


* End the round wholly within your opponent&apos;s Deployment Zone. 


* Kill 10+ models in one round.


* Have a Command Unit survive at the end of the game and be on the battlefield.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="4th Militärgrenze Division (Sarajevo)" id="27dd-b3ca-2d82-5ec1" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="2" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Osigurana Pozicija" id="d05b-b59b-5956-2362" hidden="false">
              <description>During deployment, select two non-Transport Vehicle Units in your army without the Forward Positions Special Rule and give it to them. 


You may use the Deployed In Advance Special Requisition without spending extra S.P.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Za Domovinu" id="0eea-962f-d3be-647f" hidden="false">
              <description>Non-Battlesuit Troop units in your army gain the Rapid Deployment Special Rule.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="21st Landwehr Infantry Division (Praha)" id="6830-37f6-dbe0-0c9e" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="3" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least one Infantry Platoons">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="2250-4111-e2c2-bb10" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Bohemian Plate" id="a2fe-e2b7-382d-628a" hidden="false">
              <description>* Troop Units in your army get Bulwark 1 if they are in at least two levels of Cover. 
* When Troop Units in your army activate their Shield Generator, they gain Bulwark 2.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Hrad Doctrine" id="6a6b-1375-7134-6518" hidden="false">
              <description>When a Ranged Attack is declared against a friendly Troop Unit benefiting from cover, you may spend 1 Supply point to increase its cover level by one.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Die Paladin-Peers Karls des Großen (München)" id="5671-105b-245b-37f3" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="4" type="upgrade">
          <categoryLinks>
            <categoryLink name="Die Paladin-Peers Karls des Großen (München)" id="4221-2f6b-269a-2a87" primary="true" targetId="7fd7-04c2-77b8-c8b1"/>
          </categoryLinks>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least three Battlesuit Units ">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="4ec9-47a4-5562-ea3b" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="3"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Blue Bloods" id="104b-b0c2-5a5b-9299" hidden="false">
              <description>Non-Battlesuit Units in this Army may not be issued Orders

At the Start of the Action phase, Non-cavalry Battlesuit Units in your army that have an Order Token may take a free Dash Action.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Ritterlichkeit" id="04aa-61e7-262f-be21" hidden="false">
              <description>When Chaim Drescher or a Knecht Battlesuit Unit performs an Attack Action, if the Model with the highest current Hitpoints in the targeted Unit exceeds the highest current Hitpoints of the Models in the Attacking Unit, that Unit may reroll all instances of 1s and 2s.


Chaim Drescher and Knecht Battlesuit Units in this army have the following Special Rule: Knightly Challenge</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Knightly Challenge" id="96b5-3504-cb03-287a" hidden="false">
              <description>Knightly Challenge: When this Unit activates, it may select an Enemy Unit to Challenge. It may only select Units that fulfill the following conditions:
* Within range of a weapon equipped to this Unit, or within 18” of this Unit.
* Eligible for a Ranged Attack.
* Not already Challenged by another Unit.


Until this Unit is destroyed or next activates, this Unit and the Challenged Unit are considered to have two levels of Obscured when they are Attacked by Units other than each other. 


This Unit may reroll 1s and 2s for Armor Penetration Checks against the Challenged Unit.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Imperial 1st Hussar Division (Budapest)" id="0229-2bcf-f71e-1361" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="5" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="This Specialization requires at least one Armor Platoon with three activations in it">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="fae0-4a12-4ae4-5f9b" field="forces" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="1"/>
                    <condition childId="fae0-4a12-4ae4-5f9b" field="a4ae-e848-77a7-6d45" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="lessThan" value="3"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="The Butchers of Bastogne" id="6b58-d44f-5ad8-583a" hidden="false">
              <description>Before performing an Attack Action with a Tracked Vehicle, you may spend 1 Supply Point to fire Explosive Shells. If you do this, select one Weapon Profile on the Activated Vehicle. This Weapon gains High Explosive for its next Attack. If the weapon has Ordnance X, or already has High Explosive, it instead gains Close In.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Disdain in Death" id="0530-d504-aad6-c9d4" hidden="false">
              <description>When a Tracked Vehicle Unit in this Army is Destroyed that has not Activated this Round, before rolling for Cook Off, Bailout, or any other effects of Destruction, it may perform a Free Attack Action. This Attack Action must Target the Unit that caused its destruction if possible, but may select another if the Attacker is out of range of all of its Weapons, or is not a Unit at all, e.g. Anti-Tank Minefield, Blast attack, etc.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="1st Royal Teuton Division (Konigsberg)" id="0495-ce03-d9cb-7377" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="6" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Auditors of Death" id="8af6-88e9-9972-a949" hidden="false">
              <description>During the Command Phase, place an additional blast token for each Engineer, Gun Tractor, or Command unit in your army. These must be split as evenly as possible between all Blast X types in your army.


Units with the Siege Subtype receive an Aim token for every Command or Engineer unit they are within 8&apos;&apos; of at the start of their activation.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Haubitzen!" id="bdef-8b02-3332-0ca6" hidden="false">
              <description>Command Units in your army gain the Adjust Coordinates Action as a Standard Action.


After a Siege Unit in your Army performs an Attack Action with an Ordnance Weapon, apply 1D5-2 Suppression Tokens to each Unit that was Attacked by that Weapon, to a minimum of 1.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="2nd Alpini Division &quot;Tridentina&quot; (Tyrol)" id="cf78-587a-5870-e103" hidden="false" import="true" sortIndex="7" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="error" type="add" value="You may not take Tracked Vehicles in this Specialization">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="7616-a9f8-6205-af0e" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="greaterThan" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Mountain Infantry" id="a8bc-367a-9c71-5686" hidden="false">
              <description>Troop Units in this Army ignore Rough Terrain.


Non-Battlesuit Troop Units with at least 5 models may Tow one Carriage.


When an Attack Action is taken against a Troop Unit in this army, if that Attack is Obscured, that Unit gains an additional level of Obscured.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule name="Di Qui Non Si Passa!" id="969c-c53c-104d-c94b" hidden="false">
              <description>Troop Units in this Army gain Warding on all Melee Weapons.

Carriage Units in this Army may receive the benefit of Light cover as if they were Troops, but may not receive any additional levels of Cover in this way.

Troop Units in this Army may shed one Suppression token when they activate their Shield Generator.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
